# ---- rayu-gateway environment ----
# Copy to .env for local runs. NEVER commit the real .env (provider keys).

PORT=8080

# Shared with the NestJS backend so the gateway verifies the same Rayu JWTs.
RAYU_JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Shared MySQL (prisma-style URL; the gateway converts it to a Go DSN).
DATABASE_URL=mysql://rayu:rayu_app_local@127.0.0.1:3306/rayu

# Redis for credit windows + top-up balance.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# --- Browser clients / CORS ---------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated list of origins allowed to call the gateway from a browser.
# Blank or "*" allows any origin.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS NOW: the CLI is not a browser and never sends a preflight, so
# this was irrelevant until Rayu Studio (rayu-web /studio) started calling the
# gateway directly from the page. Studio needs BOTH halves of corsMiddleware:
#   • the allowed REQUEST headers (X-Rayu-Token, X-Rayu-Upstream-URL,
#     X-Rayu-Request-Id, X-Rayu-Logical-Request-Id, X-Rayu-Query-Source,
#     X-Rayu-Intended-Model, anthropic-version, anthropic-beta) — a header missing
#     from that list fails the preflight and presents as the whole feature being
#     broken, not as one dropped header;
#   • the EXPOSED response headers (x-rayu-credits-*, x-rayu-limit, …) — without
#     them fetch() hides the values and Studio can stream a reply but never show
#     the credit balance it just spent.
# Both lists are compiled in (corsAllowHeaders / corsExposeHeaders in
# internal/server/server.go); only the ORIGIN list is configured here.
#
# SET THIS EXPLICITLY IN PRODUCTION. The "*" default happens to work today only
# because Studio's fetches are credential-less (Bearer token in a header, never
# cookies). If credentials are ever added, "*" becomes invalid and the browser
# refuses every response, so an explicit allow-list is the correct posture.
# deploy/docker-compose.yml already sets this to ${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}.
#   production: GATEWAY_CORS_ORIGINS=https://rayucode.com
#   + Vercel previews:  https://rayucode.com,https://<preview>.vercel.app
GATEWAY_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# --- Provider API key encryption ---------------------------------------------
# Provider API keys are stored in MySQL, encrypted with AES-256-GCM, and are
# decrypted by the gateway once per config refresh. This is the master key that
# opens them, and it MUST be byte-for-byte the SAME value as the backend's
# RAYU_PROVIDER_SECRET — the backend writes the envelopes, the gateway reads them.
#
#   generate:  openssl rand -base64 48        (minimum 32 characters)
#
# The gateway REFUSES TO START if provider keys exist and this is missing or
# wrong, because every hosted request would otherwise fail with no visible cause.
# ROTATION WARNING: changing this value makes every stored key undecryptable —
# they must be re-entered in the admin dashboard.
RAYU_PROVIDER_SECRET=

# --- Upstream providers -------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING about providers lives in this file any more. Base URL, wire format,
# auth scheme, the enable switch AND the API keys themselves are all managed from
# the admin dashboard (Providers page) and stored in MySQL.
#
# Adding a provider is: create it in the dashboard, add one or more API keys to
# it, done — no restart, no deploy. Changes are picked up within
# CONFIG_REFRESH_SECONDS. Several keys per provider are rotated by priority with
# automatic failover: a 429 puts that key on a short cooldown, a 401/403 takes it
# out of rotation until an admin replaces it.

# Development ONLY: allow provider base URLs that are plain http and/or point at
# a private/loopback host (e.g. a local Ollama). Off by default because the
# provider key is sent to that URL. The backend honours the same variable when
# validating admin input.
# ALLOW_INSECURE_PROVIDER_BASE_URL=1

# Optional tuning
#
# CONFIG_REFRESH_SECONDS is the SAFETY NET, not the normal path: the dashboard tells
# the gateway to re-read its configuration the moment an admin saves (admin-only
# POST /v1/_reload), and the gateway relays that notice to its other replicas over
# Redis pub/sub. The timer only covers a missed notice (Redis blip, a write made
# outside the dashboard), so it can stay comfortably long.
CONFIG_REFRESH_SECONDS=30
USER_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=10

# Redis pub/sub channel used to relay "an admin changed the configuration" between
# gateway replicas. Only has to MATCH across replicas sharing a Redis; nothing
# outside the gateway publishes to it. Blank = rayu:config-changed.
# RAYU_CONFIG_CHANNEL=rayu:config-changed
